   "source": [
    "# Final Report: Self-Supervised Image Classification using I-JEPA on BigEarthNet-S2\n",
    "\n",
    "**Author:** [Your Name]\n",
    "**Date:** 2025\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "Automated land-cover classification from satellite imagery is a critical task for environmental monitoring, urban planning, and agriculture [1]. Traditional supervised approaches require large amounts of labeled data, which is expensive to obtain for remote sensing applications. Self-supervised learning (SSL) offers a compelling alternative by leveraging unlabeled data to learn robust representations.\n",
    "\n",
    "This project applies the **Image Joint-Embedding Predictive Architecture (I-JEPA)** [2] to the BigEarthNet-S2 dataset [3], a large-scale benchmark for remote sensing image understanding. We compare I-JEPA features against a standard **ResNet-50** baseline [4] using regularized logistic regression classifiers, and rigorously evaluate the difference via 10x10 repeated stratified cross-validation and the Wilcoxon signed-rank test [5]."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "See `notebooks/01_eda.ipynb` for full visualizations. Key findings:\n",
    "- **Class imbalance**: BigEarthNet-S2 exhibits a long-tailed distribution with dominant classes such as *Arable land* and *Pastures*.\n",
    "- **Multi-spectral nature**: The dataset contains 10 Sentinel-2 bands at varying spatial resolutions (10m, 20m, and 60m).\n",
    "- **Normalization strategy**: Per-band mean/std normalization was computed on the training subset to standardize heterogeneous radiometric ranges."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Feature Extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 I-JEPA Architecture\n",
    "We implemented a simplified I-JEPA model consisting of:\n",
    "- A **Context Encoder**: Vision Transformer (ViT-Small) adapted for 10-channel 120x120 patches.\n",
    "- A **Target Encoder**: Exponential Moving Average (EMA) of the context encoder with stop-gradient.\n",
    "- A **Predictor**: Lightweight ViT that predicts target patch representations from context patches.\n",
    "\n",
    "Training was performed for 100 epochs with AdamW, cosine learning rate schedule, and mixed precision on an NVIDIA H200 GPU.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2 Baseline: ResNet-50\n",
    "We adapted a pretrained ImageNet ResNet-50 by replacing the first convolutional layer to accept 10 input channels. The backbone was frozen and used to extract 2048-dimensional embeddings.\n",
    "\n",
    "*AI-assist prompts used for code generation are documented as comments in the corresponding Python source files (`src/models/ijepa_adapter.py`, `src/models/resnet_baseline.py`).*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Hyperparameter Optimization\n",
    "\n",
    "Using **Optuna** [6], we searched the regularization parameter $C$ of a multinomial Logistic Regression classifier applied to both embedding sets. The search space was $C \in [10^{-4}, 10^{2}]$ (log-uniform). Optimization used 5-fold stratified cross-validation with macro F1-score as the objective.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Optimization Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import pickle\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import optuna\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('reports/hpo/best_params.json', 'r') as f:\n",
    "    best = json.load(f)\n",
    "print('Best hyperparameters:')\n",
    "for model, params in best.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {model}: C={params['best_C']:.6f}, F1={params['best_score']:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot optimization history\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "for ax, model in zip(axes, ['ijepa', 'resnet50']):\n",
    "    with open(f'reports/hpo/study_{model}.pkl', 'rb') as f:\n",
    "        study = pickle.load(f)\n",
    "    optuna.visualization.matplotlib.plot_optimization_history(study, ax=ax)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'{model.upper()} HPO')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Statistical Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "We performed **10 repetitions with 10 folds** (100 total fits per model) stratified cross-validation using the best $C$ found above. Scores were compared with the **Wilcoxon signed-rank test** (non-parametric, paired)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from scipy.stats import wilcoxon\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('reports/hpo/cv_scores.csv')\n",
    "scores_a = df['ijepa_f1_macro']\n",
    "scores_b = df['resnet50_f1_macro']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"I-JEPA:  {scores_a.mean():.4f} ± {scores_a.std():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"ResNet-50: {scores_b.mean():.4f} ± {scores_b.std():.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "stat, p = wilcoxon(scores_a, scores_b)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nWilcoxon signed-rank test: statistic={stat:.2f}, p-value={p:.6f}\")\n",
    "alpha = 0.05\n",
    "if p \u003c alpha:\n",
    "    print(f\"Result: Statistically significant difference at α={alpha} (p \u003c {alpha}).\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Result: No statistically significant difference at α={alpha}.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Boxplot\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "sns.set_style('whitegrid')\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(data=df[['ijepa_f1_macro', 'resnet50_f1_macro']])\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Macro F1-Score')\n",
    "plt.title('10x10 Repeated Stratified CV: I-JEPA vs. ResNet-50')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. t-SNE Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "To qualitatively assess the learned representations, we projected the I-JEPA embeddings into 2D using **t-SNE** [7] and color-coded points by their ground-truth single labels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.manifold import TSNE\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load embeddings\n",
    "data = np.load('data/processed/ijepa_embeddings.npy', allow_pickle=True)\n",
    "X = data['embeddings']\n",
    "y = data['labels']\n",
    "label_names = data['label_names']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subsample for speed if needed\n",
    "if len(X) \u003e 5000:\n",
    "    idx = np.random.choice(len(X), 5000, replace=False)\n",
    "    X_sub = X[idx]\n",
    "    y_sub = y[idx]\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    X_sub, y_sub = X, y\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Running t-SNE...')\n",
    "tsne = TSNE(n_components=2, perplexity=30, n_iter=1000, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "X_2d = tsne.fit_transform(X_sub)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "scatter = plt.scatter(X_2d[:, 0], X_2d[:, 1], c=y_sub, cmap='tab20', alpha=0.7, s=10)\n",
    "plt.legend(handles=scatter.legend_elements()[0], labels=label_names, title='Classes', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n",
    "plt.title('t-SNE of I-JEPA Embeddings (BigEarthNet-S2)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
